  "historical_output_text": " When I turned thirty-five this last October and began a long-term teaching engagement, my excitement to impart knowledge, engage students' minds to their fullest capacities through the wonders contained between my pages and those in the books, grew exponentially in direct measure with a burgeoning confidence that had, in my estimation and to some measure my superstitition, only come about by a year of turning my age.\nOne day during the week leading towards mid term exams I asked each and everyone, the entire room's 40 orso students to select their best two essays. They would read the pieces they deemed worthy to me and to one or a group within their peers for their evaluation of style (grammar included and excluding) structure. They were not, as some might believe a pedantic and constrictivive approach but rather I hoped it would engendre an atmosphere",
